---
> # Session 64 extension: $MAKE-style `pre_cmd(...)` for tests that
> # need a native compile step or a ghc-pkg invocation.  Adds two tests:
> #  - T6106 (pre_cmd '$MAKE T6106_prep' + extra_files ../shell.hs):
> #    expands $MAKE T6106_prep to a single `ghc --make T6106_preproc
> #    -v0` invocation against the deployed stage2 ghc-real on the PPC
> #    host (semantically identical to upstream's Makefile target).
> #    `../shell.hs` (a peer of scripts/) is staged into the test dir
> #    by listing it as an explicit `../shell.hs` extras entry — the
> #    existing staging loop's `cp "$SCRIPTS_DIR/$x" "$dest/"` resolves
> #    the `..` and cp picks up the basename `shell.hs`.
> #  - T19650 (pre_cmd '$MAKE T19650_setup' = `ghc-pkg latest base >
> #    my_package_env` + extra_hc_opts '-package-env my_package_env -v1'
> #    + filter_stdout_lines): uses v0.15.0's newly-deployed
> #    /opt/ghc-stage2/bin/ghc-pkg.  Pre-v0.15.0 the deployed stage2
> #    didn't include ghc-pkg (the cross-build produced an arm64 ghc-pkg
> #    via the same patch-0010 carve-out hole that v0.14.1 fixed for
> #    unlit); v0.15.0 adds `ghcPkg` to that carve-out and ships a real
> #    ppc ghc-pkg in the deployed bin/.  normalise.py gains a
> #    `--filter-stdout-regex` flag mirroring upstream's
> #    `filter_stdout_lines(...)` annotation.
> # ghci056 (pre_cmd $MAKE) is ghciNNN-shaped so belongs to session
> # 56's runner, not this one — out of scope.
